Z||000011||Oreif||07-04-2000||11:52 PM||||Cliff,<BR>The remote is great. When cruising down the highway you can adjust volume or search thru radio stations without reaching for the radio or taking eyes off the road. The other feature I like is you can attenuate the volume instead of turning the volume down for things like drive thru's. The other cool thing is if someone next to you has on their music up loud (and you don't like their taste in music)and it's a Pioneer head unit, You can hit the attenuate button and they have to disconnect the battery to reset the stereo (unless they have a remote) Or you can start changing their radio stations.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>~Oreif~<BR>Fieroholic and proud of it!||||reg||1
Z||000012||286SE'S||07-05-2000||01:15 PM||||The Daytona dash is beautiful. I have tried contacting them twice in the last month and have had no reply from them. Do you have to got through a dealer to get their products?<BR>My interior could use an update.<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000013||Oreif||07-05-2000||02:10 PM||||I just called their 1-800-226-7035 and ordered it. Prices are $160 with glovebox piece and $150 without. (aftermarket glovebox)<P>------------------<BR>~Oreif~<BR>Fieroholic and proud of it!||||reg||1
Z||000014||My7Fieros||07-05-2000||04:16 PM||||Now thats good looking Oreif! I just did the woodgrain thing on mine w/ the shelf paper...sounds corny, but it really turned out nice! I'll post pics soon. <BR>By the way Oreif and Cliff, I have that exact same stereo in one of my 86 Se's. I love it! Unfortunantly, the steering wheel remote has managed to run off somewhere..prob. hiding in one of the trunks of the other Fieros...prob. should go look for it! ||||reg||14
